   "text": "The drawing shows a pregna-1,4-diene-3,20-dione steroid with these features:\n\n- a 9-fluoro group;\n- an 11-hydroxyl;\n- a 21-hydroxyl on the C(=O)CH2OH side chain;\n- a 16-methyl;\n- no hydroxyl at C17, only the side chain.\n\nThis is desoximetasone (17-deoxy dexamethasone).\n\nThe drawing is flipped relative to the usual steroid orientation, with ring A on the right and the wedges inverted. Reading the wedges and hashes with that in mind gives the usual configuration:\n\n- 9\u03b1-fluoro;\n- 11\u03b2-hydroxyl;\n- 16\u03b1-methyl;\n- \u03b2 side chain at C17;\n- \u03b2 methyls at C10 and C13.\n\nI derived the stereodescriptors by taking dexamethasone's SMILES and replacing its C17 hydroxyl with a hydrogen. I did not independently re-derive them from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1C[C@H]2[C@@H]3CCC4=CC(=O)C=C[C@@]4([C@]3([C@H](C[C@@]2([C@H]1C(=O)CO)C)O)F)C"
